      "beats": [
        "Namaste, my little friend! Almost all of us live in a family. The family is the fundamental and most ancient unit of any society. But did you know there are different types of families? Let's explore them!",
        "In Indian society today, there are several types of families. The two most common are joint families and nuclear families. Look at this big house on the left — it is a joint family home, where many generations live together under one roof.",
        "A joint family has several generations living together — grandparents, parents, uncles and aunts, brothers, sisters and cousins. That is a lot of people! Imagine the love and laughter in this house during festivals. Everyone shares everything — food, work, joys, and sorrows.",
        "Now look at the smaller house on the right. This is a nuclear family home. A nuclear family is limited to a couple and their children, and sometimes one parent and children. It is a smaller, more intimate unit.",
        "In a nuclear family, only parents and children live together. The house is smaller, but the bonds are just as strong. Many couples in modern cities choose nuclear families because of jobs and space. Both types of families have their own advantages!",
        "So remember: a joint family has grandparents, parents, uncles, aunts, and cousins all living together. A nuclear family has just parents and children. Both are beautiful — the love is the same, only the size is different. In our next story, we will learn about roles and responsibilities in a family. Ready? Let's turn the page…"
      ]
